# Scratch copies made while testing — index.html spliced with a different
# embedded document. Never meant to be committed.
_*.html

# Documents saved out of the app. A saved Splitpage project is a whole copy
# of index.html with your script inside it, so committing one by accident
# publishes the script as well as the app.
*.splitpage.html
data/

# The server's own clone (DEPLOY.md). deploy.sh keeps the live documents,
# their snapshots and the settings file — the owner key — inside the clone it
# pulls into, so all three must stay invisible to git or a `git pull` there
# would trip over them, and a stray `git add` could publish them. (data/ is
# also ignored anywhere, above; this says so for the root on purpose.)
/data/
/backups/
/.env

# Session hand-off notes — per-session scratch, not project documentation.
# The durable equivalents are README.md, docs/help.md, DEPLOY.md, HANDOFF.md.
.claude/handoff/

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# The app itself, and a build output: `node build.mjs` writes it from src/,
# docs/help.md and VERSION. It was tracked until #80, where 1.4MB of generated
# HTML in every pull request diff — and a pre-commit hook nothing installed to
# keep it honest — stopped being worth it. CI builds it and uploads it as the
# `splitpage-app` artifact; `node package.mjs` builds it before packaging; the
# Dockerfile's first stage builds it inside the image build, so a server
# deploy needs no copy of its own (DEPLOY.md).
#
# Not being tracked is also what retired the hook's second job: a copy of the
# app with YOUR script saved into it is now an untracked local file, so there
# is nothing to accidentally commit and nothing to push.
#
# sw.js is deliberately NOT here. It cannot be inlined into the page (a worker
# needs its own URL), so it is the file you edit as well as the one that
# ships; the build only stamps its cache name from VERSION.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: desktop/tabstrip/index.html is a
# hand-written source file and must stay tracked.
/index.html

# Built releases. `node package.mjs` regenerates the lot.
dist/

# Written by the launcher at runtime so the app can show an update notice.
update-status.json

# Staged updates, and the backup an apply rolls back to.
.update/

# Build-time downloads (the bundled Node runtime). Fetched on demand.
.cache/

# npm installs. build.mjs gained one devDependency (esbuild) in #66; the
# desktop shell has its own. Neither belongs in the repo.
node_modules
